{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1140736-venomous-bite","id":1140736,"title":"Venomous Bite","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-16T00:43:38-07:00","id":1140736,"title":"Venomous Bite","content":"When I initially looked through the early backer version of C20, the Venomous Bite thingie from that one merit stood out to me as so overpowered I was sure it had to be a typo: the damage was listed as 3L on the initial bite, then 1L every turn for 6 hours. With a turn being 3 seconds, that's a LOT of damage, definitely more than I would have thought reasonable for a 5 point merit. Sure it can be soaked, but not everything can soak Lethal in the first place, and even someone who can is bound to have enough bad soak rolls out of THOUSANDS of rolls to be virtually guaranteed to die from this thing if they're not, say, Garou or something (hooray regeneration).<br /> <br /> But no - when I got the final public version of the C20 pdf the other day (with the fancy book version on its way), the Venomous Bite is STILL listed as 3L on the initial bite, 1L per turn for 6 hours. Is that really how it's supposed to be? 20L per minute, 1200L per hour, 7200L in six hours. I might have expected it from the Nagah... (And honestly, if I was told to make 7200 soak rolls, I'd just give in and let it kill me. I can make a new character in less time than that would take.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16912-fjordymcfjord","name":"FjordyMcFjord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16912_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T05:29:20-07:00","id":1140779,"title":"","content":"As it is a Chimerical damage that would affect the Chimerical side of Changelings (and Chimerical creatures), then yes, most creatures could soak it, as Changelings can soak Chimerical Lethal with their stamina. But that is beyond the point, anything that gives 3L plus a lethal per turn for 6 hours and has no in game cost (I believe he could bite the poor bastard many times) is definitely OP.<br /> <br /> About the venom power, a 3L opening damage (soakable) is not bad, considering that any weapon would do more or less the same. The post-effect of the venom I would change, for sure, cause it is beyond ridiculous. Or is it fast but short or slow but long-lasting. Maybe change the difficulty to soak it, depending on the venom.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or I would house rule to make the player who wants this Merit to choose which animal he is emulating and adapt the venom to be closer of that animal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T06:22:08-07:00","id":1140793,"title":"","content":"This is the preferable option in my opinion.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1140736-venomous-bite?p=1140779#post1140779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or I would house rule to make the player who wants this Merit to choose which animal he is emulating and adapt the venom to be closer of that animal.</div> </div> </div> </div>That being said I do believe the &quot;correct&quot; mechanism they were after would have been 3L initial damage and then 1L/h for 6 hours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}